_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{a}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052212/assets/24ca4823d220c3eb31127ed28ab7c75b1297e10ae20a1926d112a234806c411e.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{a}{3})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331871 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331872 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1041 "field-1" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331871 13194139535110 true] [17592186331870 1110 #uuid "edca3d9a-6e67-574a-bf14-4a747126ce77" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331871 1034 "\\frac{8\\pi}{3}" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535110 true] [17592186331871 1111 #uuid "7111d14f-4cea-5273-975f-a5fb19e721fc" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331872 1034 "\\frac{4\\pi}{3}" 13194139535110 true] [17592186331872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535110 true] [17592186331872 1111 